      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I contacted Adrian after a recommendation from a good friend. The quotation process was fast and easy. Adrian answered my many technical questions and provided excellent detailed advice.  We ordered a 3 phase system comprising 27 KW of panels and a 20 KW inverter, with all the required wiring and switching for batteries at a later stage. There was a delay of a few weeks in the installation of the panels due to Tilston's high workload at the time, but that really suited us because we had to dig a 100 metre trench for the underground cable from the site of the panels to the grid connection point before we could connect the solar. Tilston's installers were very efficient and easy to deal with despite the difficulties of our rural site.  The system was up and going in a few days and is performing very well, delivering 20.8 KV when necessary but it even delivers 8 KV on an overcast day, enough to run our 10 HP 3 phase bore pump. Our last power bill before going solar was $6,200 for 3 months. Now Origin is charging us about $5 per day on average, about $450 for 3 months - and it is currently winter. We are thinking about a battery and an EV now as we are putting about 40 KwH into the grid each day for 5 cents per KwH in June and we will probably double that in summer.  We are very happy with the new solar system and the after-sales service from Tilstons,",
